  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). ALL FOUR NAMED MEMBERS ARE DONE (WI-golov, WI-lalip, WI-rakol, WI-zugof), but the family statement STILL FAILS on two live instances. Status stays violated.\n\nChecked against default-settings surveys today (fixture, and koel via `hypergumbo run`):\n\n1. HOLDS NOW: node supply_chain sub-fields. The spec (§ supply_chain, line ~1101 and the example at ~1104) lists exactly the 8 emitted keys: tier, tier_name, reason, is_test_file, is_example_file, is_config_file, is_generated_file, is_exported. The \"production functions\" derivation is stated in `test-coverage --help`.\n\n2. STILL FAILS, `limits.supply_chain`: it is emitted on every run (`{}` in both surveys) and declared in docs/schema.json (`SupplyChainLimits`), but the spec's `limits` section never names it (no hit for limits.supply_chain / SupplyChainLimits in docs/hypergumbo-spec.md). WI-zugof, closed done, filed exactly \"analyzer_version/max_tier_applied/supply_chain emitted but undocumented in spec and schema\"; the spec half landed for the first two and not for supply_chain.\n\n3. STILL FAILS, `limits.max_tier_applied`: the spec (line ~1366) says it is \"recorded when a `--max-tier N` filter was applied ... null/absent when no tier filter was applied\". A DEFAULT run with no --max-tier emits `max_tier_applied: 3`. cli.py:11833 sets it to `effective_tier` unconditionally inside the filter block, and the default tier-4 exclusion is a filter. The spec describes a state the tool never emits.\n\nBoth are doc-sync instances of this family's exact statement. Recorded here rather than filed separately; the owner may prefer a residual row."  # 91be
